WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.410
Today we are flipping the script and having you ask us

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.050
any questions that you want.

3
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.050
So who's ready for some Q and A?

4
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.620
Or we like to call it.

5
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.443
Drew and A.
(audience applauds)

6
00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:13.020
With Ross!

7
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.870
All right. Let's get started.

8
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.250
First up is Vicky. Where's Vicky?

9
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.770
Hi Vicky.
Hi. Hi Drew, hi Ross.

10
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.940
Hi Vicki. I love that you stand up.

11
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:25.380
It's so, like scholastic.

12
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.680
It's like show and tell, right?

13
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.210
Yeah, totally.
Yeah.

14
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.950
Vicky, what is your question?

15
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.970
So I have a four year old. He loves to draw.

16
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:36.150
Markers, crayons, paint, anytime he sees something

17
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.100
that he can draw with he starts drawing.

18
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.600
So I got a couple of his drawings here.

19
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.433
Oh.

20
00:00:41.433 --> 00:00:43.690
He's so proud when he draws them.

21
00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:47.750
He gives them to me and he says, "Mom, look,

22
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.440
don't you love it?"

23
00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.310 line:15%
I have no idea what these are.
(Ross laughs)

24
00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:55.250 line:15%
I don't even know what to say,

25
00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:00.250 line:15%
because I couldn't even tell you what he was thinking.

26
00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.250
Can you help me figure this out?

27
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.643
Mm-hmm. Yeah.
(audience laughs)

28
00:01:09.721 --> 00:01:11.293
(Vicky laughs)

29
00:01:11.293 --> 00:01:13.543
I'm getting potato people

30
00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:18.090
that are actually like walking in the snow

31
00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.080
or some type of trail, and like those two are hanging back

32
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.360
and the other two have made it forward or?

33
00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:29.360
Oh yeah. I was getting like a solar system at first.

34
00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.700
You know what I mean?

35
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.464
Ooh, celestial?

36
00:01:32.464 --> 00:01:33.930
Yes. Like the, yeah, the-

37
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.880
Go to the next one.

38
00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.590
The next one.
All right.

39
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.850
I mean, I see an airplane.

40
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:42.080
Okay. I see the inside of a refrigerator.

41
00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.323
Like the ingredients, you know what I mean?

42
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.720
This is like a weird Rorschach test, isn't it?

43
00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.400
It is.
Yeah.

44
00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.290
Also, I you're an attorney?

45
00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.230
I am.

46
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:55.780
Well, you know, you just need to negotiate here

47
00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.290
in this situation.
Mm-hmm.

48
00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:01.890
Maybe ask him some questions

49
00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.160
about what's in his mind when he's drawing them.

50
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:05.993
Okay.

51
00:02:05.993 --> 00:02:09.230
Yeah. Or buy him a book about Jackson Pollock, right?

52
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.030
That's a great idea. Okay, thank you.

53
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.270
Great. And you may have the next big artist.

54
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.548
You might have Ban Rowe in the family.

55
00:02:16.548 --> 00:02:18.847 line:15%
(audience applauds)
Thanks Vicky.

56
00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:21.930 line:15%
(upbeat theme music)

